{
  "comment": [
    "Catalogue of installed browsers Browser Commander can import from (issue",
    "#114). Each entry says where a browser keeps its profiles on every",
    "platform, how its Chromium Safe Storage key is named, and how the OS",
    "records it as the default browser, so profile discovery, cookie",
    "decryption and `browser: 'default'` resolution are all data-driven and",
    "identical across JavaScript, Python and Rust.",
    "",
    "Root templates use these placeholders, expanded per platform:",
    "  {home}          the user home directory",
    "  {appSupport}    {home}/Library/Application Support (darwin only)",
    "  {localAppData}  %LOCALAPPDATA% (win32 only)",
    "  {appData}       %APPDATA% / roaming (win32 only)",
    "  {config}        {home}/.config (linux only)",
    "A browser with \"singleProfile\": true keeps its data in the root itself",
    "(one profile named \"Default\"); otherwise the root holds Chromium profile",
    "subdirectories (Default, Profile 1, ...) or a Firefox profiles.ini.",
    "",
    "This file is shared, not translated: Python and Rust ship byte-identical",
    "copies, checked by scripts/check-shared-fingerprint-assets.sh."
  ],
  "browsers": [
    {
